{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>Stubborn.</b> He turns aside from the way." "<b>And rebellious.</b> He is defiant regarding his father's words — a term like מַמְרִים (Deuteronomy 9)." "<b>And they shall discipline him.</b> They warn him in the presence of three and flog him (Sifrei; Sanhedrin 71a). A stubborn and rebellious son is not liable until he steals and eats a תַּרְטֵימַר of meat and drinks half a log of wine, as it is said ״זוֹלֵל וְסֹבֵא״, and it is said (Proverbs 23) ״אַל תְּהִי בְּסֹבְאֵי יַיִן בְּזֹלְלֵי בָשָׂר לָמוֹ״. And a stubborn and rebellious son is executed on account of his end — the Torah reached to the end of his understanding: in the end he will squander his father's money and seek his upkeep and not find it, and stand at the crossroads and rob people. The Torah said: let him die innocent and not die guilty (Sifrei; Sanhedrin 71a)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:47:56.005893078Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}